{title: 670 - We Give Thee But Thine Own}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #670 • SCHUMANN • 6.5.8.6}
{lyricist: William Walsham How}
{composer: Mason and Webb's Cantica Laudis}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 670}
{meta: tune SCHUMANN}
{meta: meter 6.5.8.6}
{meta: category Sentences and Responses - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]We give Thee [C/G]but [D]Thine [G/D]own,
[G]Whate’er the [D#/A#]gift [A7]maybe;
[D/A]All [Em/B]that [G]we [C/G]have [D/A]is [G]Thine [F#dim]alone,
[G]Atrust, [Am/C]O [Em/B]Lord, [D/A]from [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
